WEBVTT

00:21.000 --> 00:22.500
This is a warning.

00:32.291 --> 00:33.541
Shimura.

00:35.416 --> 00:37.333
Shimura!

00:40.541 --> 00:41.583
Aki.

00:44.166 --> 00:45.125
Are you okay?

00:45.958 --> 00:46.791
Sorry.

00:47.625 --> 00:49.416
I lost a fight.

00:50.000 --> 00:51.291
You idiot.

00:51.375 --> 00:52.958
I couldn't care less.

00:55.458 --> 00:56.291
A warning?

00:56.375 --> 00:57.666
To you?

00:58.166 --> 01:01.000
Maybe it was people jealous of our fame.

01:01.083 --> 01:02.333
I don't get it.

01:03.833 --> 01:05.833
Do I smell alcohol?

01:05.916 --> 01:08.000
You must be imagining things.

01:08.083 --> 01:09.541
I'm still a minor.

01:09.625 --> 01:13.333
Hey, next time you worry Aki, I'm gonna--

01:13.416 --> 01:14.708
Something smells fishy.

01:14.791 --> 01:16.291
Do I smell that bad?

01:16.375 --> 01:18.583
Things are lining up too perfectly.

01:18.666 --> 01:19.750
I agree.

01:19.833 --> 01:23.291
Maybe the hacker
and your attackers are the same guys.

01:23.375 --> 01:24.541
Oh, them.

01:24.625 --> 01:26.041
But how did they do it?

01:26.125 --> 01:28.583
They'd need our ID and password.

01:28.666 --> 01:30.125
I'm stumped.

01:30.625 --> 01:33.458
How did they get
their hands on our password?

01:33.541 --> 01:35.125
That's a great point.

01:37.333 --> 01:38.375
Kanegon.

01:38.875 --> 01:41.291
Did you get caught
in a porn phishing scam?

01:41.375 --> 01:42.583
Of course not.

01:42.666 --> 01:44.666
Don't make me out to be a pervert.

01:46.208 --> 01:49.500
Hey, Kanegon. Give me some editing tips.

01:49.583 --> 01:50.625
You want to learn?

01:50.708 --> 01:51.750
I do!

01:51.833 --> 01:53.583
Guess I have no choice.

01:53.666 --> 01:54.958
Yay! I'm so happy!

01:55.041 --> 01:57.875
V-i…

01:57.958 --> 02:00.500
r-a-l…

02:01.000 --> 02:03.166
H-i-t.

02:03.250 --> 02:04.583
And the password?

02:04.666 --> 02:06.708
K-K-D…

02:07.958 --> 02:09.916
What? What's wrong?

02:10.000 --> 02:11.000
Nothing.

02:12.250 --> 02:13.250
Nothing's wrong.

02:17.833 --> 02:20.208
HIGH SCHOOL

02:23.291 --> 02:25.375
Great time last night, Kanegon.

02:25.458 --> 02:26.625
Great time, my ass.

02:26.708 --> 02:28.750
If you want their contact info…

02:28.833 --> 02:30.000
The password.

02:31.250 --> 02:32.291
You stole it.

02:33.208 --> 02:35.291
I have no idea what you're talking about.

02:35.375 --> 02:36.916
Don't play dumb with me.

02:37.000 --> 02:40.416
You got our account suspended,
and had two guys ambush Shimura.

02:40.500 --> 02:43.375
Ambush?
Why would I do something like that?

02:45.250 --> 02:48.666
I've been busy with projects
since I joined an agency.

02:48.750 --> 02:49.583
Bye.

02:49.666 --> 02:51.041
Hold on!

02:53.500 --> 02:54.958
Ugh, damn it.

02:55.500 --> 02:57.333
What do I do now?

02:59.416 --> 03:01.208
-Hey.
-Hi.

03:02.041 --> 03:04.125
-What happened?
-Huh?

03:04.208 --> 03:05.458
Right here.

03:06.458 --> 03:07.791
Oh, this?

03:08.333 --> 03:10.166
Were you in a fight again?

03:10.250 --> 03:13.250
Uh, no. I kinda got ambushed.

03:13.333 --> 03:16.125
I couldn't take on two guys.

03:16.208 --> 03:17.500
Who did this?

03:17.583 --> 03:18.708
I don't know.

03:18.791 --> 03:21.916
But don't worry.
I'll get my revenge next time.

03:24.166 --> 03:27.125
I forgot to give this back to you
the other day.

03:27.208 --> 03:28.041
Thank you.

03:28.666 --> 03:29.500
Thanks.

03:37.416 --> 03:38.250
Hey.

03:39.458 --> 03:43.125
I was wondering when we can go
to the café like we promised.

03:43.208 --> 03:45.000
Oh… That's right.

03:45.083 --> 03:46.250
I'll text you.

03:47.166 --> 03:48.375
I'll go on ahead.

03:48.458 --> 03:50.208
I'll be right there.

03:57.041 --> 03:58.208
I KNOW WHO DID IT

03:58.291 --> 03:59.291
Kanegon?

04:02.625 --> 04:03.500
So…

04:04.041 --> 04:07.291
I heard Viral Hit's account got hacked.

04:07.791 --> 04:08.625
Is that so?

04:09.458 --> 04:11.083
Was it you, Mr. Kimishima?

04:11.750 --> 04:13.208
Of course not.

04:14.250 --> 04:17.083
But that's great.
They're not your problem anymore.

04:18.291 --> 04:19.125
Yeah.

04:20.125 --> 04:23.708
But I still want more followers.

04:24.208 --> 04:25.791
I know.

04:27.958 --> 04:28.833
I told you.

04:28.916 --> 04:31.750
I'll do anything for you, Rumi.

04:46.000 --> 04:47.625
Influencer agency?

04:47.708 --> 04:50.041
Yeah. Rumi recently joined an agency.

04:50.125 --> 04:50.958
This is it.

04:55.791 --> 04:56.833
Is that Rumi?

04:56.916 --> 04:59.291
That's not important. Keep scrolling.

05:04.083 --> 05:05.791
It's them. They attacked me.

05:05.875 --> 05:07.791
I knew it.

05:08.291 --> 05:10.625
Now, all the dots are connected.

05:10.708 --> 05:13.833
We need to solve this case ASAP
so I can redeem myself to Aki.

05:14.333 --> 05:15.958
To Aki? Why?

05:17.916 --> 05:18.875
Why Aki?

05:18.958 --> 05:21.708
Because I have a crush on her, obviously.

05:23.333 --> 05:26.458
Don't act surprised. You didn't notice?

05:26.541 --> 05:27.958
Um, no.

05:28.041 --> 05:29.000
Geez.

05:29.083 --> 05:30.416
We're going to Aki's.

05:31.833 --> 05:33.166
Time for an emergency meeting.

05:36.750 --> 05:38.541
Back up. Since when?

05:40.416 --> 05:44.583
They're nuisance streamers
with only 600 subscribers.

05:44.666 --> 05:47.916
Are you saying
that Rumi sent them after me?

05:48.000 --> 05:51.291
Rumi denied it,
but there's no doubt they're connected.

05:51.375 --> 05:53.791
She stole the password
and gave it to them!

05:54.708 --> 05:56.250
We need to report this to the police.

05:56.333 --> 05:57.875
This is clearly a crime.

05:59.041 --> 06:00.750
I get how you feel,

06:00.833 --> 06:04.083
but if we do that,
our channel could get taken down.

06:06.208 --> 06:09.791
The streaming app we use
is taking off with young people,

06:09.875 --> 06:12.375
but since it's so new,
it's basically anarchy.

06:12.875 --> 06:14.916
That's why we get to do what we want.

06:15.000 --> 06:17.791
If they realize
we make money off of violence,

06:17.875 --> 06:19.958
they'll ban our account immediately.

06:20.625 --> 06:23.250
Are you saying we should just let this go?

06:23.791 --> 06:24.625
No…

06:25.250 --> 06:27.500
Looks like we've got our next opponent.

06:28.833 --> 06:32.125
You intentionally fell for their trap,
right Kanegon?

06:33.208 --> 06:36.041
But they're a two-man team.

06:36.541 --> 06:38.375
I was caught off guard yesterday.

06:38.916 --> 06:42.375
We'll deal with
the repeat nuisance streamers.

06:43.125 --> 06:45.083
That should rake in money.

06:46.833 --> 06:49.166
HOW TO BEAT A THUG IN A FIGHT

06:49.250 --> 06:51.666
Is this really enough for me to win?

07:00.166 --> 07:03.166
How am I supposed to fight two guys?

07:06.666 --> 07:07.708
NEW VIDEO ALERT

07:10.958 --> 07:12.916
HOW TO WIN AGAINST MULTIPLE OPPONENTS

07:13.000 --> 07:13.833
Yes!

07:15.958 --> 07:20.708
What happens when a person
with zero training in martial arts

07:20.791 --> 07:23.166
tries to fight multiple opponents at once?

07:23.250 --> 07:25.625
He will definitely not win.

07:25.708 --> 07:29.833
But I know you're gonna show me
a new technique anyway.

07:29.916 --> 07:32.958
If you are serious about winning,

07:33.041 --> 07:36.041
you must master
at least ten of my techniques.

07:36.125 --> 07:37.375
Ten?

07:37.458 --> 07:39.000
That's kind of a lot…

07:39.083 --> 07:39.916
Exactly.

07:40.000 --> 07:44.333
In other words, there's no chance
for a beginner like you to win.

07:44.416 --> 07:47.833
If you're going up
against multiple opponents,

07:47.916 --> 07:49.750
forget about winning.

07:49.833 --> 07:51.750
Huh? Are you serious?

07:52.500 --> 07:54.500
You've gotta give me something.

07:54.583 --> 07:55.791
However,

07:55.875 --> 08:00.541
even if you can't win the fight,
you can still win the game.

08:02.125 --> 08:03.458
URABE GENERAL HOSPITAL

08:03.541 --> 08:06.291
I'm glad to hear he's enjoying school.

08:06.791 --> 08:10.625
He's made some good friends,
and he's been really lively lately.

08:10.708 --> 08:13.291
Seems like your son is enjoying his youth.

08:13.375 --> 08:15.000
He is in high school.

08:15.083 --> 08:18.000
He might even find a girlfriend.

08:18.583 --> 08:19.833
Yes, I'm aware.

08:19.916 --> 08:20.916
Morning, Doctor.

08:21.708 --> 08:24.041
-Morning.
-Good morning, Director.

08:25.125 --> 08:27.541
Looks like you're feeling better today.

08:27.625 --> 08:29.583
Today is a good day.

08:29.666 --> 08:30.500
Don't worry.

08:30.583 --> 08:33.583
You can trust us. We're in this together.

08:34.166 --> 08:35.000
Yes.

08:39.166 --> 08:42.291
The director is such a kind man.

08:45.916 --> 08:47.625
KABUKICHO

08:47.708 --> 08:48.750
Hello!

08:48.833 --> 08:49.708
-Pink!
-Green!

08:49.791 --> 08:51.083
That's us!

08:51.166 --> 08:53.916
Tonight we're gonna
prank people out on the town.

08:54.875 --> 08:57.541
Who'll give us the best reaction?

08:57.625 --> 08:59.375
It's showtime!

08:59.458 --> 09:00.833
Hey, what about her?

09:00.916 --> 09:02.500
Yo! He went for it!

09:04.541 --> 09:05.375
Hey, miss!

09:05.958 --> 09:07.333
Is this your snake?

09:07.416 --> 09:08.291
Run!

09:09.208 --> 09:10.041
Better run!

09:10.125 --> 09:11.458
Go on, run!

09:14.458 --> 09:15.833
Hey, you bastards!

09:16.791 --> 09:18.958
That's enough of your bullshit.

09:23.416 --> 09:25.333
Time to go live.

09:27.458 --> 09:28.541
DID HE GET TALLER?

09:28.625 --> 09:30.000
IT'S A GROWTH SPURT LOL

09:30.666 --> 09:33.416
Aren't you the guy from Viral Hit?

09:33.500 --> 09:34.958
What are you doing here?

09:36.750 --> 09:38.000
GET 'EM, SHIMURA! LOL

09:38.083 --> 09:39.000
TOO FUNNY LOL

09:39.083 --> 09:43.041
Starting the Viral Hit live stream!

09:48.750 --> 09:51.708
How to win against multiple opponents.

09:52.208 --> 09:55.375
The answer lies in nature.

09:56.083 --> 09:59.375
You need to bluff
and show some fighting spirit!

10:00.125 --> 10:04.541
The bluff of a mantis,
fending off an attacker for survival!

10:05.041 --> 10:10.166
The fighting spirit of a gorilla,
defending its rank in the hierarchy!

10:11.166 --> 10:14.250
Now, it's time to show them.

10:14.333 --> 10:18.333
Show them you can beat them
even though you're on your own!

10:18.416 --> 10:20.500
I was caught off guard last time,

10:20.583 --> 10:24.291
but I don't need any help
taking you fools down.

10:25.416 --> 10:27.000
The bluff of a mantis!

10:27.666 --> 10:31.875
Leave the new password
and get lost before I kill you!

10:31.958 --> 10:33.791
The fighting spirit of a gorilla!

10:33.875 --> 10:36.875
Hold on. We're in the middle of a stream.

10:39.250 --> 10:40.333
However,

10:40.416 --> 10:43.458
you must never forget this crucial point.

10:43.541 --> 10:46.291
Don't ever let your opponent catch on

10:48.208 --> 10:50.583
to your bluff and fighting spirit.

10:52.166 --> 10:53.875
You idiot, what're you doing?

10:53.958 --> 10:55.583
Yo, check it out!

10:55.666 --> 10:58.875
Look at all the insoles in his shoes!

11:01.500 --> 11:03.291
Yo, dipshit.

11:03.791 --> 11:05.500
Are you screwing with us?

11:06.708 --> 11:07.875
Don't fuck with us.

11:07.958 --> 11:08.791
What's this?

11:09.375 --> 11:11.916
Crap.
I can't hear TOU-KEI's voice anymore.

11:12.000 --> 11:13.125
What should I do?

11:13.625 --> 11:15.125
Stop it. I said stop!

11:17.083 --> 11:18.541
We're screwed.

11:18.625 --> 11:19.583
Cut it out!

11:19.666 --> 11:20.708
His shoulder!

11:20.791 --> 11:22.833
Look what he had packed!

11:22.916 --> 11:24.333
SHOULDER PADS ARE SO 80S

11:24.416 --> 11:25.500
THIS IS HILARIOUS

11:31.833 --> 11:33.916
I can't stand guys like you.

11:34.875 --> 11:36.083
No more mercy.

11:36.166 --> 11:37.666
Time for a beat-down.

11:39.875 --> 11:40.875
You fucking twerp!

11:45.250 --> 11:46.750
Damn it! That hurt!

11:46.833 --> 11:48.166
-Take that!
-Hey!

11:48.666 --> 11:49.708
Piece of shit!

11:49.791 --> 11:52.500
Huh? Something's wrong…

11:53.916 --> 11:55.791
-We need to break it up.
-Wait.

12:02.583 --> 12:04.666
What's happening to me?

12:07.625 --> 12:09.458
Stop right there!

12:12.291 --> 12:13.791
You're going nowhere!

12:14.500 --> 12:16.875
I'm scared to death…

12:18.416 --> 12:20.250
so why am I so excited?

12:25.458 --> 12:30.291
VIRAL HIT

12:37.750 --> 12:38.708
Stop!

12:39.208 --> 12:40.291
Stop, damn it!

12:41.750 --> 12:43.958
Stop running, you bastard!

12:53.208 --> 12:55.375
Get him already!

12:56.750 --> 12:58.458
Get over here, you bastard!

13:00.500 --> 13:01.625
Hey, stop!

13:13.208 --> 13:14.500
Calf kick!

13:14.583 --> 13:15.416
Calf kick!

13:15.500 --> 13:16.541
Ow!

13:18.250 --> 13:20.250
Stop! Don't you run!

13:36.583 --> 13:38.291
Calf kick!

13:44.291 --> 13:45.958
You dipshit…

13:46.875 --> 13:48.541
You're gonna pay for this.

13:48.625 --> 13:50.541
That's enough!

13:53.041 --> 13:54.833
The winner is clear.

13:55.416 --> 13:57.833
Huh? Who the hell are you?

13:58.750 --> 14:02.791
You should know better than anyone
how exhausted you are.

14:02.875 --> 14:04.000
Fuck you.

14:04.750 --> 14:06.333
This isn't over.

14:06.416 --> 14:08.875
Okay. Please proceed…

14:10.166 --> 14:13.250
to make fools of yourselves
in front of the whole world.

14:14.416 --> 14:15.750
MISSED THE BEST BIT LOL

14:15.833 --> 14:17.041
KEEP UP, CAMERAMAN!

14:21.500 --> 14:24.041
Hand over the password and go home.

14:26.291 --> 14:27.125
Shit.

14:33.708 --> 14:35.125
PASSWORD CHANGE COMPLETE

14:35.208 --> 14:36.833
Now, we're back in business.

14:37.333 --> 14:38.833
I changed the password.

14:38.916 --> 14:42.125
I didn't expect you
to put up this good of a fight.

14:42.208 --> 14:45.291
I thought we were screwed
when they ganged up on you.

14:45.375 --> 14:48.000
I have this feeling that maybe…

14:48.500 --> 14:49.750
I've gone crazy.

14:51.375 --> 14:53.500
I don't quite understand it myself.

14:54.000 --> 14:58.041
I was scared during the fight,
but also wasn't.

14:58.125 --> 15:01.500
It was like… I felt excited.

15:01.583 --> 15:04.208
What the hell? Are you okay, man?

15:04.833 --> 15:06.458
Maybe not.

15:09.916 --> 15:15.291
We're sorry for worrying you about
the sudden suspension of our main channel.

15:15.375 --> 15:18.875
Some weirdos had hacked into our channel.

15:19.375 --> 15:24.291
We've uploaded today's fight from
my temporary channel to the main channel.

15:24.791 --> 15:27.625
Please support us with donations.

15:29.500 --> 15:30.833
And, cut!

15:31.333 --> 15:32.541
How are the donations?

15:32.625 --> 15:34.333
They're flooding in!

15:34.416 --> 15:35.250
All right!

15:35.833 --> 15:37.541
Yup, and I made that happen.

15:37.625 --> 15:40.583
The audacity. You got scammed.

15:41.083 --> 15:41.916
I'm sorry.

15:45.000 --> 15:48.416
Kanegon, who's my next opponent?

15:58.333 --> 16:00.125
How long are you gonna be?

16:00.625 --> 16:01.500
Move, damn it!

16:05.791 --> 16:07.166
I died.

16:07.250 --> 16:08.958
Your turn's over.

16:09.041 --> 16:10.708
Get outta the way!

16:13.791 --> 16:16.166
What's your problem, punk?

16:16.250 --> 16:17.833
Trying to be like Viral Hit?

16:21.541 --> 16:22.708
Gimme 100 yen.

16:23.291 --> 16:24.125
What?

16:28.416 --> 16:29.625
You okay, man?

16:34.000 --> 16:35.291
VIRAL HIT

16:37.291 --> 16:39.458
VIRAL HIT
#3 RECOMMENDED VIDEO

16:41.458 --> 16:42.791
You little shit!

16:42.875 --> 16:47.291
VIRAL HIT
#1 TOP PICK VIDEO

16:49.708 --> 16:51.125
Viral Hit…

16:57.708 --> 16:59.375
I'll put your clothes here.

16:59.458 --> 17:00.291
Thank you.

17:00.375 --> 17:01.208
Sure.

17:01.791 --> 17:04.333
Say, have you heard of "streamers"?

17:05.875 --> 17:10.500
This says kids nowadays want to be
streamers when they grow up.

17:11.583 --> 17:13.208
Is that right?

17:14.333 --> 17:16.250
#1 DREAM JOB FOR BOYS:
STREAMER

17:16.333 --> 17:18.125
It's not for me.

17:18.208 --> 17:19.250
Of course not.

17:19.333 --> 17:21.666
Who would watch you stream?

17:21.750 --> 17:22.666
You're right.

17:22.750 --> 17:23.750
Oh.

17:23.833 --> 17:25.583
Maybe I should give it a try.

17:25.666 --> 17:27.708
Nobody's gonna watch that for sure.

17:27.791 --> 17:28.708
Yeah?

17:28.791 --> 17:30.625
I think I'd be great.

17:30.708 --> 17:33.291
I'd be the mom battling an illness.

17:37.041 --> 17:37.916
Say…

17:39.333 --> 17:41.958
What do you think about
people who do that?

17:43.958 --> 17:45.250
Why do you ask?

17:45.333 --> 17:48.291
Uh… I just wanted to ask.

17:50.125 --> 17:52.500
I don't see anything wrong with it.

17:53.625 --> 17:54.666
But

17:55.333 --> 17:57.166
I'm sure the parents are worried.

17:58.916 --> 18:02.125
I'd rather my child
work a normal job like you do.

18:04.458 --> 18:05.333
I see.

18:07.750 --> 18:08.583
Oh.

18:09.333 --> 18:10.916
I need to get going.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.125
Always so busy. Do you have work today?

18:13.208 --> 18:14.208
Uh, no…

18:14.916 --> 18:16.166
I have a thing.

18:16.791 --> 18:18.625
Are you going on a date?

18:19.458 --> 18:21.666
Of course not.

18:21.750 --> 18:24.166
Really? That's a shame.

18:30.208 --> 18:31.541
VIRAL HIT

18:31.625 --> 18:35.458
Calling all opponents!
Self- and third-party nominations welcome!

18:35.541 --> 18:37.833
All right, it's uploaded.

18:37.916 --> 18:39.583
Wow.

18:39.666 --> 18:41.541
It's already got views.

18:42.333 --> 18:43.916
What's he up to?

18:44.416 --> 18:47.208
Who knows?
He just said he couldn't come today.

18:47.708 --> 18:48.750
He had work?

18:48.833 --> 18:49.958
Nope.

18:50.750 --> 18:51.583
Huh?

18:52.458 --> 18:54.333
He's out with Asamiya.

18:54.416 --> 18:57.041
He begged me to spare him just for today.

18:57.125 --> 18:59.166
I bet he's planning to profess his love.

19:02.416 --> 19:03.666
Hey, did you realize

19:04.333 --> 19:06.500
it's just the two of us here.

19:06.583 --> 19:09.416
This makes me kinda nervous, you know?

19:14.541 --> 19:17.083
So Aki, do you have a boy--

19:20.916 --> 19:23.791
Keep your hands off of my daughter.

19:23.875 --> 19:25.291
I would never…

19:27.541 --> 19:29.166
I don't trust you.

19:29.250 --> 19:31.791
Oh, come on. Don't say that, Dad?

19:31.875 --> 19:32.875
Dad?

19:33.375 --> 19:34.291
Aki.

19:34.916 --> 19:38.250
I'm glad you made friends,
but why are they always boys?

19:38.333 --> 19:40.291
Shut up and get back to work.

19:44.750 --> 19:46.166
Hey.

19:50.250 --> 19:51.250
Sorry about that.

19:51.333 --> 19:53.416
Don't worry about it. I get it.

19:54.000 --> 19:57.541
Living abroad long-term
makes you sound blunt, right?

19:57.625 --> 20:00.541
No, he was dead serious.

20:01.916 --> 20:02.750
Oh.

20:04.208 --> 20:06.583
Where were you before returning to Japan?

20:06.666 --> 20:07.750
The United States.

20:07.833 --> 20:10.541
Wow, that's pretty cool.

20:10.625 --> 20:15.125
I lived there for 12 years
due to my dad's job, but I never fit in.

20:51.916 --> 20:54.125
Are you sure you didn't mind paying?

20:54.208 --> 20:56.500
I wanted to return the favor.

20:57.000 --> 20:57.958
Thank you.

20:59.083 --> 21:00.416
The parfait was good.

21:00.500 --> 21:01.583
Yeah.

21:01.666 --> 21:04.875
So what was it
you wanted to talk to me about outside?

21:05.416 --> 21:06.250
Right.

21:07.125 --> 21:08.208
So, um…

21:08.833 --> 21:10.875
I can't find the courage in me…

21:12.250 --> 21:13.541
Asamiya.

21:14.958 --> 21:16.791
You live in a huge house.

21:17.500 --> 21:19.625
What the hell am I saying?

21:20.250 --> 21:21.750
The other day,

21:22.666 --> 21:24.958
I followed you
to return your handkerchief.

21:25.833 --> 21:28.166
I promise I wasn't stalking you.

21:28.666 --> 21:30.208
Yeah, I know.

21:30.958 --> 21:31.833
It just…

21:32.708 --> 21:35.166
We live in completely different worlds.

21:36.250 --> 21:38.291
Your dad must be very important.

21:38.791 --> 21:40.875
No, he's just a regular guy.

21:41.916 --> 21:43.666
But why would you have to work?

21:43.750 --> 21:45.541
It's just a part-time job.

21:45.625 --> 21:47.250
Yeah, you're right.

21:47.916 --> 21:49.416
That was your question?

21:49.500 --> 21:50.333
Uh…

21:51.833 --> 21:52.750
No.

21:53.250 --> 21:54.666
Not exactly.

22:18.375 --> 22:19.666
Maybe next time.

22:21.666 --> 22:22.958
Sure. Got it.

22:37.708 --> 22:38.958
Guys!

22:41.541 --> 22:43.375
I found your next opponent!

22:43.458 --> 22:44.375
Really? Who?

22:44.458 --> 22:47.958
Reo Shinjo.
He's a former high-school taekwondo champ.

22:48.041 --> 22:49.458
Taekwondo?

22:50.041 --> 22:53.125
Our viewers are
hyped that you're fighting him.

22:54.458 --> 22:57.458
Now he's a high school dropout
turned troublemaker.

22:58.041 --> 23:02.041
Rumor says he fights so much
that he doesn't bother to fix his watch.

23:02.541 --> 23:04.166
It's a hot match-up, right?

23:04.250 --> 23:06.875
I can practically smell the money.

23:06.958 --> 23:08.875
-Hold on…
-It's too reckless.

23:09.541 --> 23:11.791
He shouldn't fight a martial artist.

23:11.875 --> 23:13.000
Exactly.

23:13.083 --> 23:15.458
Sorry, but we can't refuse this offer.

23:15.541 --> 23:18.000
The reason why our viewers are so hyped

23:19.416 --> 23:20.833
is because he volunteered!

23:20.916 --> 23:22.041
@REOSHINJO FIGHT ME

23:25.750 --> 23:26.583
IT'S HIM!

23:26.666 --> 23:27.875
SHINJO FOUND YOU!

23:27.958 --> 23:28.875
GAME OVER LOL

23:28.958 --> 23:29.791
No way…

23:36.583 --> 23:38.083
-Asamiya?
-Yes?

23:40.708 --> 23:41.833
Did you see this?

23:41.916 --> 23:44.250
VIRAL HIT'S HOT GIRLFRIEND!

23:44.875 --> 23:45.833
How did this…

23:45.916 --> 23:49.875
Looks like someone figured out
who you are from the video

23:49.958 --> 23:52.000
on Hamaken TV and Viral Hit.

23:52.500 --> 23:53.583
FOUND TRUE BEAUTY!

23:53.666 --> 23:54.500
WIFE MATERIAL

23:54.583 --> 23:56.166
You should be careful.

23:56.666 --> 24:00.041
Let me know if any weirdos come,
and I'll tell the manager.

24:00.625 --> 24:01.458
Okay.

24:03.958 --> 24:06.500
Don't let the test results bring you down.

24:07.166 --> 24:08.916
Your numbers will improve.

24:10.833 --> 24:12.541
Whoa, awesome!

24:12.625 --> 24:13.541
He won again!

24:13.625 --> 24:15.791
Keep it down. This is a hospital.

24:16.291 --> 24:17.750
Don't worry about it.

24:18.291 --> 24:20.291
Oh, that looks fun.

24:20.375 --> 24:21.750
What are you watching?

24:21.833 --> 24:22.666
Viral Hit.

24:22.750 --> 24:24.666
He's a super popular streamer.

24:24.750 --> 24:26.916
This is what's popular now, huh?

24:27.416 --> 24:30.083
I'm gonna be a streamer
when I grow up too.

24:30.166 --> 24:32.333
Nice. I hope you do that.

24:33.333 --> 24:34.833
Thank you.

24:42.208 --> 24:43.666
ASAMIYA: THAT WAS FUN

24:43.750 --> 24:44.666
SEE YOU AT WORK

24:48.291 --> 24:49.208
What's up?

24:49.291 --> 24:50.625
Shimura! Where are you?

24:51.208 --> 24:52.833
I'm on my way to work.

24:52.916 --> 24:54.500
Aki's in serious trouble!

24:59.833 --> 25:01.416
Don't make me repeat myself.

25:02.125 --> 25:03.666
Shimura won't fight you.

25:03.750 --> 25:05.083
I wasn't asking you.

25:05.166 --> 25:06.625
That's enough. Let's go.

25:06.708 --> 25:07.625
Let go of me.

25:08.125 --> 25:11.625
Our viewers are egging us on
because you put your name down.

25:11.708 --> 25:12.875
Take it back.

25:12.958 --> 25:14.583
Don't tell me what to do.

25:15.125 --> 25:16.708
Aki, please. Let's just go.

25:16.791 --> 25:18.500
Aki, are you all right?

25:19.875 --> 25:21.041
Did you call him?

25:21.125 --> 25:22.916
-Sorry.
-That was uncalled for.

25:23.000 --> 25:24.166
Let's go home, Aki.

25:24.250 --> 25:25.416
Hold on.

25:28.000 --> 25:28.875
Fight me.

25:32.083 --> 25:35.041
Sorry, but you're way too strong
for me to take on.

25:35.125 --> 25:36.000
Then…

25:39.625 --> 25:41.333
give me your channel.

25:41.416 --> 25:42.583
What?

25:46.208 --> 25:47.041
Kanegon!

25:47.708 --> 25:49.333
I know you're making bank.

25:51.750 --> 25:52.666
I want it.

25:55.500 --> 25:56.708
You must be joking.

25:58.000 --> 25:58.833
Stop it!

26:07.750 --> 26:09.000
I said stop!

26:19.208 --> 26:20.250
Give it to me!

26:21.250 --> 26:23.083
Stop it! You're gonna kill him!

26:25.916 --> 26:26.750
Let go!

26:35.291 --> 26:36.291
Damn it!

26:39.791 --> 26:41.416
Okay!

26:42.333 --> 26:44.291
You can have our channel.

26:45.458 --> 26:47.208
So please, just stop.

26:57.375 --> 26:58.708
Make an announcement.

27:00.458 --> 27:02.250
Say that it's mine now.

27:19.291 --> 27:23.375
I heard streaming is becoming
a popular career path among young people.

27:24.625 --> 27:25.750
That's right.

27:26.250 --> 27:27.333
Now it's a socially--

27:27.416 --> 27:31.041
It's a cop-out for losers
who can't land a real job.

27:39.333 --> 27:41.583
RUMI
72,000 FOLLOWERS

27:43.375 --> 27:44.208
Here.

27:45.125 --> 27:47.625
I'm not gaining many followers lately.

27:48.958 --> 27:50.416
It happens sometimes.

27:50.916 --> 27:52.291
What should I do?

27:54.625 --> 27:58.708
Getting you exposure
and promoting you costs money.

28:00.166 --> 28:03.916
If you take on more jobs,
we could afford the costs.

28:04.500 --> 28:07.166
That's no problem.
I can take on more jobs.

28:07.250 --> 28:08.541
Really?

28:08.625 --> 28:13.083
That would definitely help,
since our sponsors take priority.

28:13.166 --> 28:14.541
What do you need me to do?

28:18.083 --> 28:19.541
A simple job.

28:24.583 --> 28:26.958
That was a disaster.

28:28.416 --> 28:31.208
Lately, dangerous guys
have been coming for us.

28:32.166 --> 28:33.083
We're

28:34.375 --> 28:36.333
just not cut out for this.

28:40.958 --> 28:42.416
I didn't agree to this.

28:43.125 --> 28:43.958
What?

28:50.250 --> 28:52.166
I didn't want to hand it over.

28:53.208 --> 28:55.750
That's our channel.

29:01.958 --> 29:04.333
When you stood up to Hamaken,

29:05.875 --> 29:06.708
I…

29:07.875 --> 29:09.916
I honestly was really moved.

29:11.291 --> 29:14.041
You made me believe
that even if we're bullied,

29:15.333 --> 29:17.125
we can make miracles happen.

29:17.625 --> 29:19.458
That it's okay to be brave.

29:20.125 --> 29:21.375
But then…

29:23.375 --> 29:25.916
Why would you
hand over our channel so easily?

29:31.333 --> 29:32.458
Is that

29:33.458 --> 29:36.541
how little you care for Viral Hit?

29:39.083 --> 29:39.958
It is.

29:41.416 --> 29:44.041
Why would I go head-to-head
with a guy like him?

29:44.916 --> 29:46.208
I'm not an idiot.

29:51.416 --> 29:52.791
Are you okay?

29:59.666 --> 30:00.625
What's wrong?

30:04.250 --> 30:05.333
I need you to leave.

30:06.166 --> 30:07.833
Why? Aki came all this--

30:07.916 --> 30:08.916
Please!

30:10.583 --> 30:11.625
Just go.

30:14.416 --> 30:15.708
Let's go, Aki.

30:31.625 --> 30:33.958
Stop it! You're gonna kill him!

30:50.000 --> 30:52.000
I'm such a loser.

30:54.166 --> 30:56.416
Once Shinjo sets his target,

30:56.500 --> 31:01.041
he roughs up their friends
rather than the target themselves.

31:02.333 --> 31:04.208
And he does it in front of them.

31:06.625 --> 31:10.000
He leaves his opponent
utterly humiliated and powerless.

31:10.500 --> 31:13.500
He's a psychopath
who gets a rush from that.

31:14.750 --> 31:16.083
And…

31:18.458 --> 31:20.041
There's a rumor

31:20.708 --> 31:23.666
that Shinjo killed
a fellow delinquent two years ago.

31:24.250 --> 31:26.583
He was released due to lack of evidence,

31:26.666 --> 31:28.541
but the killer remains at large.

31:28.625 --> 31:31.375
That's how dangerous he is.

31:33.958 --> 31:37.375
I won't fight someone like that.

31:52.375 --> 31:54.708
That's our channel.

31:56.916 --> 31:57.916
Is that

31:59.000 --> 32:02.166
how little you care for Viral Hit?

32:20.291 --> 32:21.666
Did you upload the video?

32:22.708 --> 32:23.666
Not yet.

32:30.125 --> 32:33.625
As promised, you can have our channel.

32:34.125 --> 32:34.958
But

32:35.041 --> 32:36.791
I've got one condition.

32:38.833 --> 32:40.125
Give me one month.

32:41.041 --> 32:43.000
It's yours if you beat me then.

32:48.916 --> 32:50.458
Give me the time and place

32:51.750 --> 32:53.250
once it's decided.

32:59.750 --> 33:01.541
So that happened.

33:03.875 --> 33:06.833
What were you thinking?
Didn't I tell you not to?

33:06.916 --> 33:07.750
I know, but--

33:07.833 --> 33:08.791
Call it off.

33:08.875 --> 33:11.250
I can't. It's a done deal.

33:14.083 --> 33:15.208
I knew it.

33:16.875 --> 33:17.708
You're a fool.

33:17.791 --> 33:19.083
Shut up.

33:19.958 --> 33:21.208
All right, I'm out.

33:21.291 --> 33:23.125
I'll be busy with training.

33:23.208 --> 33:24.875
Wait, Shimura!

33:26.416 --> 33:29.666
You might not walk away
with just injuries this time.

33:30.458 --> 33:32.291
Why would you do this?

33:35.541 --> 33:37.125
For the money, of course.

33:42.708 --> 33:43.791
More time off?

33:44.375 --> 33:46.916
But you just took a whole month off!

33:47.000 --> 33:48.833
Yes… I'm sorry.

33:48.916 --> 33:51.250
How long do you need
to take off this time?

33:52.333 --> 33:53.708
About a month…

33:53.791 --> 33:57.583
Are you secretly going on
a short-term study abroad program?

33:57.666 --> 33:59.750
I mean, who takes long leaves from--

33:59.833 --> 34:00.666
I'm sorry!

34:00.750 --> 34:02.958
Huh? Where do you think you're going?

34:04.916 --> 34:06.083
Shimura!

34:06.166 --> 34:07.166
Asamiya.

34:07.250 --> 34:09.625
I talked to the manager about your shift.

34:10.125 --> 34:11.958
Sorry for all the trouble.

34:12.041 --> 34:12.875
It's fine.

34:13.750 --> 34:15.625
Is this for another fight?

34:16.125 --> 34:16.958
Yeah.

34:17.541 --> 34:20.375
Don't worry.
I've got someone I can rely on.

34:21.208 --> 34:22.208
I see.

34:22.291 --> 34:23.125
Yeah.

34:23.833 --> 34:25.750
But would you still fight

34:26.750 --> 34:29.916
if this ally of yours was no longer here?

34:30.541 --> 34:33.000
Huh? Why would you ask that?

34:33.083 --> 34:36.625
I mean, you keep fighting
tougher and tougher opponents.

34:36.708 --> 34:37.625
I'm worried.

34:38.125 --> 34:40.291
Oh… Thanks.

34:42.250 --> 34:43.125
Say.

34:43.958 --> 34:47.750
Do you think we could go out
for tea again after my next stream?

34:47.833 --> 34:52.083
I want to tell you
what I couldn't last time.

34:54.750 --> 34:55.791
Of course.

34:56.583 --> 34:57.583
Promise?

34:59.500 --> 35:01.416
Yeah, I promise.

35:01.500 --> 35:02.333
Okay.

35:16.750 --> 35:17.708
Taekwondo?

35:18.250 --> 35:20.750
I was wondering how I could win.

35:21.416 --> 35:22.250
Well…

35:23.666 --> 35:27.750
If you can shut down his kicks,
you might have a shot at winning.

35:27.833 --> 35:29.958
Shut down his kicks?

35:30.041 --> 35:34.750
But it's not something a novice like you
can accomplish in a month.

35:36.833 --> 35:38.208
Yeah, I figured.

35:38.708 --> 35:41.750
Hey! Tatsuya! Time for a spar!

35:41.833 --> 35:42.666
Okay.

35:43.250 --> 35:44.375
Sorry to interrupt.

35:44.458 --> 35:46.250
It's okay. Come back anytime.

35:48.500 --> 35:49.375
Here.

35:50.333 --> 35:51.791
-Ready?
-Ready.

35:59.666 --> 36:01.375
Nothing…

36:11.583 --> 36:12.500
He's here, sir.

36:14.833 --> 36:15.791
That's him.

36:20.375 --> 36:21.750
BAD FELLOWS, huh?

36:21.833 --> 36:22.750
What's that?

36:22.833 --> 36:23.791
Seriously?

36:24.458 --> 36:27.541
It's a popular show
where amateur fighters fight.

36:29.500 --> 36:31.541
Are you Shimura from Viral Hit?

36:31.625 --> 36:32.958
Uh, yes.

36:36.000 --> 36:38.250
I'm the organizer of BAD FELLOWS,

36:39.291 --> 36:40.291
Kuwata.

36:41.250 --> 36:42.958
Yes, I know who you are.

36:43.458 --> 36:44.750
That makes things easy.

36:44.833 --> 36:46.041
What do you say?

36:47.041 --> 36:49.708
Would you be interested
in coming on our show?

36:49.791 --> 36:50.916
What?

36:51.000 --> 36:53.750
You have the potential
to become even more famous.

36:58.541 --> 37:00.666
Sorry, but I'm not interested.

37:03.041 --> 37:08.333
I don't want to be a professional fighter,
and I'm not looking for fame either.

37:09.458 --> 37:10.458
I see.

37:12.333 --> 37:15.333
Well, if you ever face financial troubles,

37:15.833 --> 37:17.375
come see me anytime.

37:17.958 --> 37:18.916
I can help.

37:33.250 --> 37:35.583
Here's your change and your receipt.

37:35.666 --> 37:36.583
The food was great.

37:36.666 --> 37:37.750
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

37:37.833 --> 37:38.916
That was yummy.

37:42.000 --> 37:43.166
Welcome!

37:45.375 --> 37:46.375
Father?

37:49.541 --> 37:51.416
VIRAL HIT'S HOT GIRLFRIEND!

37:54.458 --> 37:56.875
You're so annoying, you piece of trash!

37:56.958 --> 37:58.791
I'm not a loser!

38:18.500 --> 38:20.916
Any more of this is too dangerous.

38:21.000 --> 38:21.833
LOGAN

38:38.500 --> 38:40.791
NEW VIDEO FROM HOW_TO_FIGHT

38:44.291 --> 38:45.125
Huh?

38:45.625 --> 38:49.583
HOW A NOVICE CAN BEAT
A TAEKWONDO FIGHTER

38:54.958 --> 38:57.125
ONE MONTH LATER

39:14.291 --> 39:15.375
Let's go.

39:20.708 --> 39:21.541
Rumor says

39:22.541 --> 39:25.458
Shinjo killed
a fellow delinquent two years ago.

39:53.375 --> 39:55.666
Huh? You're gonna run?

39:56.166 --> 39:57.083
He's fast!

40:12.541 --> 40:14.833
Fighting mindset, rule one.

40:16.625 --> 40:18.083
Make him lose his cool.

40:18.166 --> 40:19.958
You little…

40:21.625 --> 40:23.166
What the hell was that?

40:24.125 --> 40:25.125
Aki, stay here.

40:25.208 --> 40:26.833
You can reach me on this.

40:27.333 --> 40:28.333
But…

40:29.916 --> 40:31.458
Leave this to me.

40:32.500 --> 40:35.166
I'm done showing you at my worst.

40:37.125 --> 40:38.458
IT'S ALREADY STARTED!

40:38.541 --> 40:39.458
GO! SHIMURA!

40:39.541 --> 40:40.833
IS HE SPRAYING WATER?

40:40.916 --> 40:42.500
I NEED YOU TO WIN, SHIMURA

40:42.583 --> 40:43.750
I'M SWEATING LOLOL

40:43.833 --> 40:45.041
IT'S HAPPENING!!!

40:59.500 --> 41:01.625
Keep your eyes shut, and you're dead.

41:02.416 --> 41:05.708
How to beat a taekwondo fighter, rule one.

41:06.833 --> 41:09.583
Dominate the space
to shut down their kicks!

41:15.666 --> 41:16.500
Dumbass.

41:16.583 --> 41:19.458
You think you can win by splashing water?

41:21.166 --> 41:23.833
As if I'd only use my foot techniques.

41:29.333 --> 41:32.250
This is supposed to be a fight, right?

41:44.625 --> 41:45.791
That's right.

41:46.375 --> 41:47.458
This is a fight.

41:51.208 --> 41:52.833
WHY ISN'T SHIMURA SLIPPING?

41:52.916 --> 41:54.416
HE'S WEARING WATER SHOES!

41:54.500 --> 41:56.000
THAT'S SNEAKY LOL

42:06.958 --> 42:09.250
It's not over yet.
The fight has barely begun.

42:19.083 --> 42:24.416
Nothing frustrates a martial artist
who specializes in kicks

42:24.500 --> 42:26.000
more than a tackle.

42:26.083 --> 42:31.916
The key to a successful tackle
is to grab the back of the knees.

42:32.000 --> 42:34.583
Pull the back of your opponent's knees,

42:34.666 --> 42:38.208
and you can take down even a big opponent!

42:38.291 --> 42:41.083
This is called the double leg tackle!

42:41.166 --> 42:42.291
Yes!

42:44.000 --> 42:50.500
If the tackle is successful,
your odds of winning go above 50 percent!

42:51.666 --> 42:56.791
But you must never
swing your fist from above!

42:57.791 --> 43:00.166
You only get one chance
against a martial artist.

43:00.250 --> 43:04.291
You must finish them off in one blow!

43:07.416 --> 43:10.250
Put your hand behind your opponent's neck,

43:10.333 --> 43:13.416
grab their collar, and pull them close!

43:22.583 --> 43:28.375
Even if they resist,
don't let go, no matter what.

43:28.458 --> 43:31.500
This technique compresses
the carotid artery.

43:31.583 --> 43:33.333
The cross choke!

43:33.416 --> 43:37.041
It takes ten seconds
for your opponent to pass out.

43:37.541 --> 43:41.541
Count the seconds in your head!

43:42.041 --> 43:43.125
One…

43:43.666 --> 43:44.500
Two…

43:45.000 --> 43:46.375
-Go!
-Three…

43:47.041 --> 43:48.125
Four…

43:49.041 --> 43:50.125
Five…

43:50.791 --> 43:51.916
Six…

43:52.500 --> 43:53.458
Seven…

43:53.958 --> 43:55.208
Eight…

43:55.708 --> 43:57.291
Nine…

43:59.041 --> 43:59.875
HUH?

43:59.958 --> 44:03.083
SHINJO DOESN'T LOOK WORRIED

44:03.166 --> 44:04.791
YOU'RE RIGHT LOLOL

44:06.333 --> 44:08.041
Oh no. He lost the choke!

44:10.625 --> 44:11.625
Dumbass.

44:12.708 --> 44:14.250
It wasn't locked in.

44:14.333 --> 44:15.541
What?

44:18.625 --> 44:19.583
Shimura!

44:20.125 --> 44:21.250
ALMOST HAD IT!

44:21.333 --> 44:22.708
YOU WERE SO CLOSE!

44:22.791 --> 44:26.208
No, Shinjo got in that chokehold
on purpose.

44:29.333 --> 44:32.083
You really think
I'd submit to your technique?

44:34.708 --> 44:36.125
This is what I wanted.

44:40.833 --> 44:44.333
The only way for a novice
to beat a taekwondo fighter

44:44.416 --> 44:47.416
is to shut down their kicks!

44:48.375 --> 44:49.958
Now I can throw my kicks.

44:52.833 --> 44:58.250
If you fail to do that,
there's only one thing left to do.

44:59.375 --> 45:01.666
Run for your life!

45:07.291 --> 45:08.125
Shimura!

45:09.083 --> 45:10.416
Get out of there!

45:13.291 --> 45:14.833
I'm a fool.

45:15.708 --> 45:18.875
All that training for nothing.

45:31.083 --> 45:31.958
Shit.

45:32.958 --> 45:34.708
He's really gonna kill Shimura.

46:18.416 --> 46:25.416
VIRAL HIT

47:43.125 --> 47:46.125
Subtitle translation by:
Kanako Connie Takahashi
